%% title: Error-triage bot — first-pass analysis in Slack
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Slack error channel
    box rgb(219,234,254) Built by me
    participant B as portal-ai error-triage bot ★
    end
    participant P as Policy (sentinel)
    participant O as OpenSearch (analysis history)
    participant G as GitLab API
    participant L as Vertex AI (LLM)
    S->>B: Error-alert thread event (Socket Mode)
    B->>B: Detect truncated message → re-fetch thread
    B->>P: Dedupe by signature (TTL policy)
    B->>B: Count repeats
    opt threshold exceeded within window
        B-->>S: 🚨 escalation warning (once)
    end
    alt duplicate
        B-->>S: 👀 reaction only (skip analysis)
    else new
        B->>O: Look up past analyses · first occurrence by signature
        B->>G: Last 5 commits per file in stack trace (circuit breaker)
        B->>L: Analyse (semaphore 2 · retry 3× on 429/5xx · backoff + jitter)
        L-->>B: First-pass analysis
        B->>O: Save analysis
        B-->>S: Thread reply (+ first-seen time · link to earlier thread)
    end
    S->>B: 👍/👎 feedback · 🔍 re-analyse · follow-up via mention
